    "result": "I fixed the bug, but I haven't run the tests. The test command needed approval and wasn't run, so the two failing checks are unconfirmed.\n\nThe bug was in `_process_case` in `sqlparse/filters/aligned_indent.py`. The condition-width calculation had its test inverted. It computed the width only when `cond` was empty, which is the `else`/`end` case where `cond` is `None`. That is what raised `TypeError: 'NoneType' object is not iterable`. It now computes the width when `cond` is present and uses 0 otherwise.\n\nTo check it, run `python -m pytest tests/test_format.py -q` from the workspace."
